==============================================================================
WARN -- Apache License 2.0 incompatibilities
Apache OpenServerless (Incubating) -- consolidated
==============================================================================

This file lists third-party components bundled anywhere in the Apache
OpenServerless distribution whose licenses are NOT compatible with the
Apache License, Version 2.0, together with components that require special
handling. It is the aggregate view; the WARN file of each submodule remains
authoritative for that component.

Classification follows the ASF third-party licensing policy:

    https://www.apache.org/legal/resolved.html

  Category A  Apache-2.0 compatible. May be included in a release.
  Category B  May be included in BINARY form only, unmodified and as a
              separate file, with the reciprocal license disclosed.
  Category X  MUST NOT be included in an Apache release artifact.

IMPORTANT SCOPE NOTE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Apache release artifact for OpenServerless is the SOURCE distribution.
It consists of Apache-2.0 licensed sources, including the vendored Apache
OpenWhisk tree under build/openwhisk, plus Dockerfiles. The published
container images and the `ops` binaries are CONVENIENCE BINARIES assembled
at build time from third-party base images, package repositories and Go and
Maven module caches. Category X components inherited from a base operating
system image are disclosed below but are not redistributed by the ASF in
source form.


==============================================================================
CATEGORY X
==============================================================================

  No Category X component is linked into or included in any release
  artifact. Two Category X components are DOWNLOADED AT RUN TIME by the end
  user as `ops` prerequisites. They are not in the source release and not
  in any published image layer.

  Component : 7-Zip standalone binary, 7zz (24.07) / 7zr.exe on Windows
  License   : LGPL-2.1-or-later, plus an unRAR field-of-use restriction
  Affects   : oplugins/prereq.yml (run-time download only)
  Action    :
      Downloaded on first use of `ops`, unmodified, as a separate
      executable, directly from upstream by the end user. Not present in
      the Apache source release and not in any published image layer, so no
      release artifact is affected. The unRAR clause is a field-of-use
      restriction and is non-free by both FSF and ASF standards. Disclosed
      here for the benefit of users; nothing to remove from the release.
      Preferred long-term fix: replace 7zz with a Category A extractor.

  Component : bun (1.3.14)
  License   : MIT (own sources) statically linked with JavaScriptCore and
              WebKit (LGPL-2.1) and tinycc (LGPL-2.1); bundles zstd
              (BSD OR GPL-2.0, BSD elected)
  Affects   : oplugins/prereq.yml (run-time download only)
  Action    :
      bun's own code is Category A, but the upstream binary is
      LGPL-2.1-encumbered through static linking and carries the LGPL-2.1
      relink obligation. Downloaded on first use, unmodified, as a separate
      executable, directly from upstream by the end user. Not present in
      the Apache source release or in any published image layer. Disclosed
      here; no action required.

  NOTE ON SCOPE
      The prerequisite download is performed by `ops -t` in
      devcontainer/start.sh, which runs as the container ENTRYPOINT. It
      executes when a container starts, not while the image is built, so
      the published docker.io/apache/openserverless-devcontainer image
      contains NEITHER of the binaries above -- they are fetched into the
      writable layer of a running container. Do NOT reintroduce a
      `RUN ops -t` step into any Dockerfile: that would bake Category X
      binaries into a published image layer.

  The `ops` CLI links 92 third-party Go modules. Every one of them resolves
  to a Category A license (Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC
  or public domain). No GPL, LGPL, AGPL or BSL component is linked into the
  released binary.


